    "text": "KJV Song of Solomon 7:9: “And the roof of thy mouth like the best wine for my beloved, that goeth down sweetly, causing the lips of those that are asleep to speak.” Hebrew (WLC) 7:10: דֹּובֵ֖ב שִׂפְתֵ֥י יְשֵׁנִֽים. Brenton’s Greek 7:10: ἱκανούμενος χείλεσί μου καὶ ὀδοῦσιν. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/SNG07.htm) prints: “suiting my lips and teeth”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/22/7/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/SNG07.htm.",
