    "summary": "The KJV of Hosea 10:14 has “Shalman spoiled Betharbel in the day of battle”. Brenton’s Greek prints a name “Σαλαμάν” and “ἐκ τοῦ οἴκου τοῦ Ἱεροβοάμ”, which Brenton’s own English gives as “out of the house of Jeroboam”.",
    "text": "KJV Hosea 10:14: “as Shalman spoiled Betharbel in the day of battle”. Hebrew (WLC) 10:14: כְּשֹׁ֧ד שַֽׁלְמַ֛ן בֵּ֥ית אַֽרְבֵ֖אל בְּיֹ֣ום מִלְחָמָ֑ה. Brenton’s Greek 10:14: ὡς ἄρχεν Σαλαμὰν ἐκ τοῦ οἴκου τοῦ Ἱεροβοὰμ, ἐν ἡμέραις πολέμου. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/HOS10.htm) prints: “as prince Solomon departed out of the house of Jeroboam, in the days of battle”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/28/10/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/HOS10.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The Hebrew quoted prints בית ארבאל after שלמן. The Greek does not print a place Betharbel; it prints “the house of Jeroboam”. The person’s name is printed in a different form in the two texts and the record does not rest on that; it rests on the second name.",
