    "text": "KJV Joel 2:32: “and in the remnant whom the Lord shall call”. Hebrew (WLC) 3:5: וּבַ֨שְּׂרִידִ֔ים אֲשֶׁ֥ר יְהוָ֖ה קֹרֵֽא. Brenton’s Greek 3:5: καὶ εὐαγγελιζόμενοι οὓς Κύριος προσκέκληται. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/JOL03.htm) prints: “and they that have glad tidings preached to them, whom the Lord has called”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/29/3/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/JOL03.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The Hebrew quoted prints ובשרידים אשר יהוה קרא. The KJV’s noun is “remnant”. The Greek prints a participle of the verb for bringing or receiving good news, which Brenton’s own English gives as “glad tidings preached”. A remnant and those who have good news preached to them are different descriptions of the group the Lord calls.",
