    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "The KJV of Joel 3:21 has “I will cleanse their blood that I have not cleansed”. Brenton’s Greek prints ἐκζητήσω for the first verb, which Brenton’s own English renders “I will make inquisition for”, and οὐ μὴ ἀθωώσω for the second.",
    "text": "KJV Joel 3:21: “I will cleanse their blood that I have not cleansed”. Hebrew (WLC) 4:21: וְנִקֵּ֖יתִי דָּמָ֣ם לֹֽא־נִקֵּ֑יתִי. Brenton’s Greek 4:21: Καὶ ἐκζητήσω τὸ αἷμα αὐτῶν, καὶ οὐ μὴ ἀθωώσω. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/JOL04.htm) prints: “And I will make inquisition for their blood, and will by no means leave it unavenged”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/29/4/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/JOL04.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The Hebrew quoted prints ונקיתי דמם לא נקיתי, the same verb twice, and the KJV renders both occurrences “cleanse”. The Greek prints two different verbs: ἐκζητήσω, then a negated verb that Brenton’s own English renders “will by no means leave it unavenged”. The KJV’s first clause promises to cleanse; the Greek’s first clause promises to seek out the blood.",
