    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "The KJV of Amos 4:4 has “your sacrifices every morning, and your tithes after three years”. Brenton’s Greek prints εἰς τὴν τριημερίαν τὰ ἐπιδέκατα ὑμῶν, which Brenton’s own English renders “your tithes every third day”.",
    "text": "KJV Amos 4:4: “and your tithes after three years”. Hebrew (WLC) 4:4: לִשְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת יָמִ֖ים מַעְשְׂרֹֽתֵיכֶֽם. Brenton’s Greek 4:4: εἰς τὴν τριημερίαν τὰ ἐπιδέκατα ὑμῶν. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/AMO04.htm) prints: “your tithes every third day”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/30/4/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/AMO04.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The Hebrew quoted prints לשלשת ימים מעשרתיכם. The KJV’s interval is three years. The Greek’s interval is a word for a span of three days (τριημερίαν), which Brenton’s own English renders “every third day”. Years and days are different units.",
