    "summary": "The KJV of Amos 7:1 has the Lord form grasshoppers “in the beginning of the shooting up of the latter growth” and “the latter growth after the king’s mowings”. Brenton’s Greek prints a swarm of locusts “from the east” and “one caterpillar”, followed by Γὼγ ὁ βασιλεύς, which Brenton’s own English renders “king Gog”.",
    "text": "KJV Amos 7:1: “he formed grasshoppers in the beginning of the shooting up of the latter growth” … “the latter growth after the king's mowings”. Hebrew (WLC) 7:1: יֹוצֵ֣ר גֹּבַ֔י בִּתְחִלַּ֖ת עֲלֹ֣ות הַלָּ֑קֶשׁ … וְהִ֨נֵּה־לֶ֔קֶשׁ אַחַ֖ר גִּזֵּ֥י הַמֶּֽלֶךְ. Brenton’s Greek 7:1: ἐπιγονὴ ἀκρίδων ἐρχομένη ἑωθινὴ, καὶ ἰδοὺ βροῦχος εἷς, Γὼγ ὁ βασιλεύς. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/AMO07.htm) prints: “a swarm of locusts coming from the east; and, behold, one caterpillar, king Gog”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/30/7/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/AMO07.htm.",
