    "text": "KJV Amos 8:1: “behold a basket of summer fruit”. Hebrew (WLC) 8:1: וְהִנֵּ֖ה כְּל֥וּב קָֽיִץ. Brenton’s Greek 8:1: Καὶ ἰδοὺ ἄγγος ἰξευτοῦ … καὶ εἶπα, ἄγγος ἰξευτοῦ. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/AMO08.htm) prints: “And behold a fowler's basket”. KJV Amos 8:2: “A basket of summer fruit”. Hebrew (WLC) 8:2: כְּל֣וּב קָ֑יִץ. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/30/8/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/AMO08.htm.",
    "reasoning": "At 8:1 the Hebrew quoted prints והנה כלוב קיץ and at 8:2 כלוב קיץ. The KJV’s basket holds summer fruit. The Greek’s vessel is ἄγγος ἰξευτοῦ, a fowler’s, a bird-catcher’s. Fruit and a fowler are different things, and the Greek has no word for summer or fruit in the phrase.",
