    "scope": "No tag is proposed: the KJV renders the Hebrew, the Greek of Joel and the Greek of Acts each faithfully in this wording, and the record compares what the two passages print. It does not say that either is mistaken, does not examine how the New Testament writer uses Joel, and does not say that Acts 2:17 is meant as a quotation of Joel’s exact words. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text; the Greek of Joel is Brenton’s printed edition of the Septuagint; the Greek of Acts is Tischendorf’s eighth edition as served by bolls.life, with the Textus Receptus there carrying the same words. None of these is a critical apparatus. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text. A digital named edition is not proof that every manuscript agrees; other Hebrew manuscripts were not examined. The Greek quoted is Brenton’s printed edition of the Septuagint, an ancient Greek translation tradition of the Old Testament. It is not a critical apparatus and does not show that all Greek witnesses agree or which reading is original. English in square brackets is the researcher’s plain rendering, not a KJV quotation and not a lexicon entry. The Greek New Testament wording is Tischendorf’s eighth edition as served by bolls.life (TISCH), compared with the Textus Receptus text served there (TR); neither is a critical apparatus.",
