    "text": "KJV Habakkuk 2:5: “because he transgresseth by wine, he is a proud man”. Hebrew (WLC) 2:5: כִּֽי־הַיַּ֣יִן בֹּוגֵ֔ד גֶּ֥בֶר יָהִ֖יר. Brenton’s Greek 2:5: Ὁ δὲ κατοιόμενος, καὶ καταφρονητὴς, ἀνὴρ ἀλαζὼν. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/HAB02.htm) prints: “But the arrogant man and the scorner, the boastful man”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/35/2/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/HAB02.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The Hebrew quoted prints כי היין בוגד גבר יהיר. The KJV gives a cause of the man’s transgression, wine, and calls him proud. The Greek prints three descriptions of a man, with a noun that Brenton’s own English renders “scorner”, and none of them is wine. A statement that wine causes the transgression and a list of the man’s attitudes are different statements.",
