    "summary": "The KJV of Zechariah 4:7 has the great mountain “become a plain” before Zerubbabel and “the headstone” brought forth “with shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto it”. Brenton’s Greek prints τοῦ κατορθῶσαι and τὸν λίθον τῆς κληρονομίας, which Brenton’s own English renders “that thou shouldest prosper” and “the stone of the inheritance”.",
    "text": "KJV Zechariah 4:7: “before Zerubbabel thou shalt become a plain” … “he shall bring forth the headstone thereof with shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto it”. Hebrew (WLC) 4:7: לִפְנֵ֥י זְרֻבָּבֶ֖ל לְמִישֹׁ֑ר … וְהֹוצִיא֙ אֶת־הָאֶ֣בֶן הָרֹאשָׁ֔ה תְּשֻׁאֹ֕ות חֵ֥ן חֵ֖ן לָֽהּ. Brenton’s Greek 4:7: τὸ πρὸ προσώπου Ζοροβάβελ τοῦ κατορθῶσαι … καὶ ἐξοίσω τὸν λίθον τῆς κληρονομίας, ἰσότητα χάριτος χάριτα αὐτῆς. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/ZEC04.htm) prints: “before Zorobabel, that thou shouldest prosper” … “I will bring out the stone of the inheritance, the grace of it the equal of my grace”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/38/4/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/ZEC04.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The Hebrew quoted prints לפני זרבבל למישר and והוציא את האבן הראשה תשאות חן חן לה. In the first clause the KJV says the mountain becomes level ground; the Greek has a verb that Brenton’s own English renders “prosper”. In the second the KJV has the stone brought forth by one who is spoken of in the third person, with shoutings, and the Greek has the speaker bring out “the stone of the inheritance” with a phrase about grace. The record does not identify who or what prospers in the Greek clause. The headstone with shoutings and the stone of the inheritance are different descriptions.",
