    "summary": "The KJV prints “tribute” at Matthew 17:24 for τὰ δίδραχμα and at 17:25 and 22:17 for κῆνσον, two different words, in both served Greek editions.",
    "text": "KJV Matthew 17:24: “they that received tribute money came to Peter”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) Matthew 17:24: οἱ τὰ δίδραχμα λαμβάνοντες [those who receive the didrachma]. Greek New Testament (Textus Receptus as served, printed there without accents) Matthew 17:24: οι τα διδραχμα λαμβανοντες [those who receive the didrachma]. KJV Matthew 22:17: “Is it lawful to give tribute unto Caesar, or not?”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) Matthew 22:17: ἔξεστιν δοῦναι κῆνσον Καίσαρι [is it lawful to give kenson to Caesar?]. Greek New Testament (Textus Receptus as served, printed there without accents) Matthew 22:17: εξεστιν δουναι κηνσον καισαρι [is it lawful to give kenson to Caesar?]. KJV Matthew 17:25: “take custom or tribute?”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) Matthew 17:25: τέλη ἢ κῆνσον. The Textus Receptus text served prints the same words. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/40/17/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/40/17/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/40/22/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/40/22/.",
