    "summary": "The KJV of Mark 7:3 says the Pharisees do not eat “except they wash their hands oft”. Tischendorf’s text prints πυκνά, “frequently”, which fits “oft”; the Textus Receptus text served prints πυγμῇ, a word for the fist.",
    "text": "KJV Mark 7:3: “except they wash their hands oft”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) Mark 7:3: ἐὰν μὴ πυκνὰ νίψωνται τὰς χεῖρας [unless they wash their hands frequently]. Greek New Testament (Textus Receptus as served, printed there without accents) Mark 7:3: εαν μη πυγμη νιψωνται τας χειρας [unless they wash their hands with the fist]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/41/7/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/41/7/.",
    "reasoning": "The two served editions print different words for the manner of the washing. The KJV’s “oft” renders the idea of frequency, which Tischendorf’s word expresses and the Textus Receptus word, on its ordinary meaning, does not.",
    "scope": "T applies at Mark 7:3. The Greek editions differ from each other here, and the KJV’s English matches only one of them: the KJV’s “oft” corresponds to the word πυκνά in Tischendorf’s text, while the Textus Receptus text served prints πυγμῇ, a word that means the fist. The sense of πυγμῇ in this verse is itself a matter of reading, and this record does not say what it means there or which wording is original. Two digital editions are not a survey of manuscripts. The Greek New Testament wording is Tischendorf’s eighth edition as served by bolls.life (TISCH), compared with the Textus Receptus text served there (TR); neither is a critical apparatus.",
