    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "The KJV of Mark 15:25 says “it was the third hour, and they crucified him”. The KJV of John 19:14 says that when Pilate brought Jesus out, on “the preparation of the passover”, it was “about the sixth hour”.",
    "text": "KJV Mark 15:25: “it was the third hour, and they crucified him”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) Mark 15:25: ὥρα τρίτη. KJV John 19:14: “about the sixth hour”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) John 19:14: ἕκτη. KJV Mark 15:33: “when the sixth hour was come, there was darkness over the whole land until the ninth hour”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/41/15/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/41/15/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/43/19/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/43/19/.",
    "reasoning": "Mark puts the crucifixion at the third hour. John puts the judgment before Pilate, which precedes the crucifixion, at about the sixth hour, which is the hour at which Mark has the darkness begin (15:33). Both verses use a named hour of the day, and the two statements can stand together only if the two writers counted the hours of the day differently or if one of the numbers has been transmitted differently; neither verse says which.",
