    "reasoning": "Mark has the passover meal eaten before the arrest. John has the passover still to be eaten after the arrest, and 19:14 calls the day of the crucifixion “the preparation of the passover”. The two accounts can both stand if “passover” in John names a later meal or the feast as a whole, or if the two accounts reckon the day differently; neither verse says which.",
