    "summary": "The KJV of Mark 16:8 says that the women who fled from the sepulchre said nothing “to any man; for they were afraid”. The KJV of Matthew 28:8 says that they “did run to bring his disciples word”, and Luke 24:9 that they “told all these things unto the eleven”.",
    "text": "KJV Mark 16:8: “neither said they any thing to any man; for they were afraid”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) Mark 16:8: οὐδενὶ οὐδὲν εἶπον. KJV Matthew 28:8: “did run to bring his disciples word”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) Matthew 28:8: ἔδραμον ἀπαγγεῖλαι τοῖς μαθηταῖς αὐτοῦ. KJV Luke 24:9: “told all these things unto the eleven, and to all the rest”. KJV Mark 16:7: “go your way, tell his disciples and Peter that he goeth before you into Galilee”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/41/16/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/41/16/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/40/28/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/40/28/.",
    "reasoning": "Mark’s verse says they said nothing to anyone. Matthew and Luke say that they told the disciples. The statements can stand together if Mark’s silence refers to the way, or to a time before they delivered the message, but 16:8 gives no limit of time or place.",
