    "title": "the casting out of those who sold in the temple: in the last week (Mark) or at the first passover of the ministry (John)?",
    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "The KJV of Mark 11:15 has Jesus begin “to cast out them that sold and bought in the temple” on the day after he entered Jerusalem for the last time. The KJV of John 2:15 has him do it when “the Jews’ passover was at hand”, early in the account, after the miracle at Cana and a short stay at Capernaum.",
    "text": "KJV Mark 11:15: “began to cast out them that sold and bought in the temple”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) Mark 11:15: ἤρξατο ἐκβάλλειν τοὺς πωλοῦντας. KJV John 2:15: “he drove them all out of the temple”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) John 2:15: πάντας ἐξέβαλεν ἐκ τοῦ ἱεροῦ. KJV John 2:13: “the Jews' passover was at hand, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem”. KJV Mark 11:11: “Jesus entered into Jerusalem, and into the temple”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/41/11/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/41/11/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/43/2/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/43/2/.",
    "reasoning": "Each passage tells of Jesus casting out the sellers from the temple. In Mark the event is in the last week and in John it is at the beginning, with a passover named in each. The two can both stand if he did it twice; neither Gospel says so, and John tells no second casting out.",
    "scope": "No tag is proposed: the record compares the wording of the passages and does not rest on a difference between the KJV and the Greek. It does not say that either account is mistaken. Where Greek is quoted, the Textus Receptus text served carries the same words. The record does not say that either account is out of order and does not examine the words said in the temple in either account. The Greek New Testament wording is Tischendorf’s eighth edition as served by bolls.life (TISCH), compared with the Textus Receptus text served there (TR); neither is a critical apparatus.",
