    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "The KJV of John 3:15 says “whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have eternal life”. The Textus Receptus text served prints μὴ ἀπόληται ἀλλ’ ἔχῃ ζωὴν αἰώνιον; Tischendorf’s text prints only ἵνα πᾶς ὁ πιστεύων ἐν αὐτῷ ἔχῃ ζωὴν αἰώνιον, “that everyone who believes in him may have eternal life”, with no “should not perish”.",
    "text": "KJV John 3:15: “should not perish, but have eternal life”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) John 3:15: ἵνα πᾶς ὁ πιστεύων ἐν αὐτῷ ἔχῃ ζωὴν αἰώνιον [that everyone who believes in him may have eternal life]. Greek New Testament (Textus Receptus as served, printed there without accents) John 3:15: μη αποληται αλλ εχη ζωην αιωνιον [should not perish but have eternal life]. KJV John 3:16: “should not perish, but have everlasting life”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) John 3:16: μὴ ἀπόληται ἀλλ’ ἔχῃ ζωὴν αἰώνιον. The Textus Receptus text served prints the same words. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/43/3/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/43/3/.",
    "reasoning": "One edition has the negative clause in 3:15 and the other does not. Both editions print “should not perish, but have” at 3:16.",
    "scope": "T applies at John 3:15. The difference is between Greek editions: the Textus Receptus text served agrees with the KJV and Tischendorf’s text does not. This record does not say which reading is original, and two digital editions are not a survey of manuscripts. The record does not say which reading is original. The preposition after “believes” also differs (εἰς in the Textus Receptus text, ἐν in Tischendorf’s); the record rests on the clause only. The Greek New Testament wording is Tischendorf’s eighth edition as served by bolls.life (TISCH), compared with the Textus Receptus text served there (TR); neither is a critical apparatus.",
