    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "The KJV of John 3:22 has Jesus come into the land of Judaea with his disciples, where “he tarried with them, and baptized”. The KJV of John 4:1 says he “made and baptized more disciples than John”, and 4:2, in a parenthesis, adds “Jesus himself baptized not, but his disciples”.",
    "text": "KJV John 3:22: “and there he tarried with them, and baptized”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) John 3:22: καὶ ἐκεῖ διέτριβεν μετ’ αὐτῶν καὶ ἐβάπτιζεν. KJV John 4:2: “Jesus himself baptized not, but his disciples”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) John 4:2: Ἰησοῦς αὐτὸς οὐκ ἐβάπτιζεν ἀλλ’ οἱ μαθηταὶ αὐτοῦ. KJV John 4:1: “Jesus made and baptized more disciples than John”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/43/3/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/43/3/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/43/4/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/43/4/.",
    "reasoning": "The subject of the verb is Jesus in 3:22 and 4:1, and 4:2 says in the next breath that he did not himself baptize. The accounts can stand together if 3:22 and 4:1 speak of the baptizing done under his authority by his disciples, which 4:2 states directly. The verses do not say so in 3:22, where the verb is simply his.",
