    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "The KJV of Matthew 3:14 has John the Baptist try to stop Jesus coming to be baptized, saying “I have need to be baptized of thee, and comest thou to me?”. The KJV of John 1:31 and 1:33 has John say twice “I knew him not”, and add that the one who sent him to baptize told him of the sign by which he would know.",
    "text": "KJV Matthew 3:14: “I have need to be baptized of thee, and comest thou to me?”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) Matthew 3:14: ἐγὼ χρείαν ἔχω ὑπὸ σοῦ βαπτισθῆναι. KJV John 1:33: “And I knew him not”. Greek New Testament (Tischendorf, eighth edition) John 1:33: κἀγὼ οὐκ ᾔδειν αὐτόν. KJV John 1:31: “And I knew him not”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/40/3/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/40/3/, https://bolls.life/get-text/TISCH/43/1/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/TR/43/1/.",
    "reasoning": "The words in Matthew are those of a man who knows who is coming and in John the same man says he did not know him before the sign. The two can stand together if “I knew him not” means that he did not know him as the one who baptizes with the Holy Ghost until the sign was given, which John 1:33 states; Matthew does not say when John received the sign.",
